{
  "summary": "Ensures all initial outbound connections (default 3) for private transaction broadcasts run to completion even if the transaction is received back from the network or becomes invalid in the mempool. Replaces immediate transaction removal upon receipt with a resolved status, preventing subsequent retry connections via TryGrantRetry while allowing scheduled initial sends to finish. Peer disconnections are tracked directly, and connection compensation in FinalizeNode checks whether the handshake succeeded rather than transaction receipt confirmation.",
  "problem": "When a privately broadcast transaction was received back from a peer before all initial connections were established, the node immediately removed the transaction and canceled any remaining unestablished connections. This introduced a timing side channel where adversaries returning a transaction quickly could suppress remaining outbound connections and correlate or deanonymize the broadcaster.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'Intended as an alternative to #34707, addressing the theoretical timing attack described in https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/34707#issuecomment-5603256702. Also fixes theoretical timing attacks described in https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/29415#discussion_r2035693786.'"
