  "card": "Ensures all three initial outbound connections for private transaction broadcasts finish even if the transaction is received back from the network while connections are still pending. Previously, receiving the transaction back immediately canceled unstarted broadcast connections, introducing theoretical timing side channels that an adversary could exploit to detect or link private broadcasts. The change marks transactions resolved to prevent retries without truncating the initial batch, and replaces receipt tracking upon peer disconnect with handshake status. It serves as an alternative to PR 34707.",
